WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:12.140
KERRY: I really love my job and what I do,
and getting to see them develop and grow

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.910
as young people and support their families
to have the best quality for these

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.490
young people is the best part of my job.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.240
And during the first lockdown, there
was a family struggling because their

00:00:25.259 --> 00:00:27.030
usual community access wasn't there.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.460
Residential was shut down.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.540
It wasn't safe for this young
person to be in school because

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:31.710
they have other medical needs.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:39.030
And what we did was arrange for
us to take one of the school cars

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.019
and go and take him for a drive
once a week, just for half an hour.

00:00:44.685 --> 00:00:50.115
He loved it because he loves roads and
maps and he was giving me directions

00:00:50.115 --> 00:00:53.415
the entire time, finding it hilarious
to drive me down dead ends and then

00:00:53.415 --> 00:00:55.785
have me reverse out thinking it was
great and I'm there and there's a

00:00:55.785 --> 00:00:59.595
big bus going, "oh my goodness, how
am I going to fit down this road?".

00:01:00.735 --> 00:01:04.875
But it gave his family a chance to sit
down and have a cup of tea or, you know,

00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:09.015
get the washing done or spend some time
with his siblings and that, but how

00:01:09.015 --> 00:01:16.770
much he loved seeing us again, after
quite a gap and how much he enjoyed

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:21.470
that time away from home as well doing
something he enjoyed was really lovely.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.390
In a mainstream setting when I used to
work in a year three class and there

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:36.990
was a young boy in there with autism,
we worked, this was before I had an

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:41.210
awful lot of knowledge of autism I will
admit, we worked really hard on getting

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:47.685
him to communicate to us when he needed
help, because he would just sit lost

00:01:47.685 --> 00:01:55.065
in a sea of about 35 children and just
just wait for you to come around to him.

00:01:55.125 --> 00:01:58.635
And the first day he picked up his
help card and held it in the air was

00:01:58.635 --> 00:02:00.465
just, oh, it was an amazing moment.

00:02:01.385 --> 00:02:05.295
It was really good, so to see him
come on and his communication and

00:02:05.385 --> 00:02:07.515
how he's doing was was fantastic.

